Built on SAGE — https://github.com/l33tdawg/sage — which is where everything
Mynah remembers is stored. Apache 2.0, same licence as this project.

Sources/SageVoiceCore contains speech-to-text code lifted from QuietType
(https://github.com/l33tdawg/quiettype), same author.

The ASR runtime depends on argmax-oss-swift (WhisperKit / TTSKit),
Copyright (c) 2024 argmax, inc. — MIT License.

whatsapp/ is derived from the WhatsApp bridge in hermes-agent
(https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent), Copyright (c) 2025 Nous
Research — MIT License, full text in whatsapp/LICENSE.hermes. The upstream
commit it was taken from, and every local change, are recorded in
whatsapp/PROVENANCE.md. It uses Baileys (https://github.com/WhiskeySockets/Baileys)
— MIT License — which is not affiliated with or endorsed by WhatsApp.

Baileys depends on libsignal (https://github.com/privacyresearchgroup/libsignal-protocol-typescript,
published to npm as `libsignal`), which is **GPL-3.0**, and it ships inside
Mynah.app in Contents/Resources/whatsapp/node_modules. This paragraph exists
because the one above it used to end at "MIT License" and was read, correctly,
as a statement that the whole WhatsApp side was permissively licensed. It was
not.

What that means here: libsignal is loaded by the WhatsApp bridge, which is a
separate program — its own `node` process, talking to Mynah over a UNIX socket
and a loopback port. Mynah conveys it rather than linking it, so the obligation
is conveyance: the GPL-3.0 text travels in the bundle at
Contents/Resources/licences/GPL-3.0.txt, libsignal's own copy stays where npm
put it, and the complete corresponding source for the version shipped is
available from the address in this file on request, for as long as this build is
distributed. No local modifications have been made to it.

scripts/package-app.sh refuses to build if a copyleft package appears in that
tree without being named here — see the licence gate. That check is new; before
it, this dependency had shipped unnoticed.
